title: Documenting every reused GobboNet element
---
date: 2026-10-18
---
author: Labyricorn
---
summary: A pinned-commit reuse inventory, source hashes, and public notices separate upstream work from what Labbonet implements itself.
---
tags: provenance, documentation
---
source_commit: 555b7c6d6b144ad6cef7562e3effa1b892c3a397
---
body:

Labbonet follows GobboNet's design closely, so the project stopped to make the
relationship explicit. The owner asked that every reused element be documented
and credited to Elodine / GoblinCorps, and that copied source, adapted behavior,
and Labbonet's own implementation be kept distinct.

The inventory is pinned to one upstream commit. Each reused CSS file was checked
against that commit, and the exact line spans and SHA-256 hashes are recorded in
a machine-readable provenance file. The old grouped reuse log became a
file-by-file record with screen and element boundaries and the points where
Labbonet's implementation begins. A root notice file, the public README, and the
in-app About view all carry the credit, and files that mix upstream and original
material say so.

The audit also corrected stale wording such as "design reference only" where
source had since been reused. Excluded behavior stays excluded: installer
logic, firewall changes, wide-open listening, recursive-delete uninstalls, and
unrestricted script hooks are never reused. The inventory is kept up to date as
material is added, changed, or removed, and the docs state that Labbonet is not
affiliated with GobboNet.

[Commit 555b7c6](https://github.com/Labyricorn/Labbonet/commit/555b7c6d6b144ad6cef7562e3effa1b892c3a397)
